        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/02/ios-27-fixes-apple-mail-in-three-ways-longtime-users-will-love/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/06/apple-mail-app-icon-ios-27.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">iOS 27 is packed with powerful features like <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/23/ios-27s-new-siri-delivers-in-every-single-way-id-hoped-for/\" data-type=\"post\" data-id=\"1061918\">Siri AI</a> and upgrades to productivity apps like <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/01/heres-everything-new-for-apple-mail-in-ios-27/\">Apple Mail</a>, <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/30/heres-everything-new-for-apple-notes-in-ios-27/\" data-type=\"post\" data-id=\"1056067\">Notes</a>, <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/26/heres-everything-new-for-reminders-in-ios-27/\">Reminders</a>, and <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/18/heres-everything-new-for-apple-calendar-in-ios-27/\" data-type=\"post\" data-id=\"1058167\">Calendar</a>. But for many users, some of iOS 27’s best changes might be bug fixes that make apps run better than ever—here are three coming to Apple Mail.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apple-mail,ios-27\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1067168\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/02/ios-27-fixes-apple-mail-in-three-ways-longtime-users-will-love/#more-1067168\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
