        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2024/06/Sequoia-intel.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple started informing developers today that universal macOS apps on the Mac App Store that require macOS 13 or later can now drop support for Intel-based Macs.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apps,macos\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1067041\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/01/apple-tells-mac-app-store-developers-they-can-now-drop-intel-support/#more-1067041\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
